CREATE TABLE results_database.id_first_occurrence
WITH (
    format='PARQUET',
    parquet_compression='SNAPPY',
    external_location='s3://your-output-bucket/id-first-occurrence/'
) AS
SELECT
    id,
    CAST(FLOOR(MIN(yr*4+qtr-1)/4) AS INTEGER) AS first_yr,
    CAST(MOD(MIN(yr*4+qtr-1),4)+1 AS INTEGER) AS first_qtr,
    CONCAT(
        CAST(CAST(FLOOR(MIN(yr*4+qtr-1)/4) AS INTEGER) AS VARCHAR),
        '-Q',
        CAST(CAST(MOD(MIN(yr*4+qtr-1),4)+1 AS INTEGER) AS VARCHAR)
    ) AS first_yr_qtr
FROM source_database.parquet_table
WHERE id IS NOT NULL
  AND TRIM(id)<>''
  AND yr IS NOT NULL
  AND qtr BETWEEN 1 AND 4
GROUP BY id;

Athena reads the ID, year, and quarter columns from every Parquet file in the selected S3 folder.
Invalid records are removed, including missing IDs, missing years, and quarters outside 1 through 4.
Each year-quarter is converted into a sortable integer using year × 4 + quarter − 1.
This conversion preserves chronological order, including the transition from the fourth quarter of one year to the first quarter of the next year.
Athena groups all records that have the same ID.
Within each ID group, Athena finds the minimum calculated quarter value.
The minimum value represents the first quarter in which that ID appears.
Athena converts the minimum value back into separate year and quarter columns.
The final dataset contains one row per unique ID with its first observed year and quarter.
Athena writes the results back to S3 as compressed Parquet files.
